 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile SpiraxSarco_RIM10_Flowmeter_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/SpiraxSarco_RIM10_Flowmeter.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "All 49 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
  "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Relay output status 1 = on/closed); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance.",
  "Units are part of the object names (e.g. Mass flow lb/min, Pressure psig) rather than the units column."
